    "abstract": "Illustrated parts breakdown of one main landing gear brake position, showing the brake filter, the accumulator kit, the torque tube hardware and the wear and temperature sensing items.",
    "sections": {
      "purpose": "This figure gives the parts breakdown of one main landing gear brake position, including the hydraulic interface and the wear and temperature sensing items. Use it to order brake hardware and sensing parts.",
      "figure_note": "The figure shows one brake position; the aircraft carries sixteen main wheel positions and the breakdown repeats at each. The swaged collars at the torque tube interface are single use and are always ordered with a brake change. Items 110 and 110A are the control unit hydraulic interface at the position and are the only items on this figure affected by the control unit requalification: item 110 is called up pre MOD-142240 and item 110A post MOD-142240. The attachment hardware at items 30 to 90 is common to both standards and is not effectivity keyed. The wear pin scale differs between heat stack standards and is not a catalogue item; refer to the applicable maintenance task for the reading procedure."
    },
